#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Render the dated competitive landscape from reviewed primary-source notes."""
import html,json,pathlib
ROOT=pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
# These maintained files are the single source of truth. Rendering must never
# replace newer evidence with a second set of hardcoded feature definitions.
landscape=json.loads((ROOT/'docs/landscape.json').read_text())
vendors=landscape['vendors']
features=json.loads((ROOT/'docs/features.json').read_text())
assert len({f['id'] for f in features})==len(features), 'Duplicate feature identity'
def esc(x): return html.escape(str(x),quote=True)
links=lambda v:' '.join(f'<a href="{esc(u)}" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Source {i+1} ↗</a>' for i,u in enumerate(v['sources']))
cards=''.join(f'''<article class="vendor"><div class="eyebrow">{esc(v['category'])}</div><h3>{esc(v['name'])}</h3><p class="price">{esc(v['price'])}</p><dl><dt>Features</dt><dd>{esc(v['features'])}</dd><dt>Difference</dt><dd>{esc(v['difference'])}</dd><dt>License</dt><dd>{esc(v['license'])}</dd><dt>Limits / uncertainty</dt><dd>{esc(v['caveat'])}</dd><dt>Source check</dt><dd>{esc(v.get('checked',landscape['reviewed']))}</dd></dl><footer>{links(v)}</footer></article>''' for v in vendors)
component=json.loads((ROOT/'benchmarks/screenpipe-keyword-http-v1.json').read_text())
component_rows=''.join(f'<tr><td>{run["records"]:,}</td><td>{esc(name)}</td><td>{run["summary"][key]["medianMS"]:.3f} ms</td><td>{run["summary"][key]["p95MS"]:.3f} ms</td><td>{run["summary"][key]["exactSets"]}/{run["summary"][key]["observations"]}</td></tr>' for run in component['runs'] for key,name in [('screenpipe','Screenpipe 0.4.53'),('oswind','OSwind a5d4af4')])
component_table='<h3>Stock Screenpipe: authored keyword HTTP</h3><p>Same authored original text, authenticated HTTP and restricted sandbox; 14 cases × five timed rounds per product and size. Both hit every positive first result and return empty for the absent control. OSwind adds a mint-paint note after the correct quiet-mint design hit. All 21 contract cases and both fresh runs pass. Screenpipe wins this observed warm component workload. <a href="SCREENPIPE-COMPARISON.md">Protocol and retained failures</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/screenpipe-keyword-http-v1.json">Raw measurements</a>.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table id="screenpipe-http"><thead><tr><th>Records</th><th>Product</th><th>Warm median</th><th>Warm p95</th><th>Exact sets</th></tr></thead><tbody>'+component_rows+'</tbody></table></div><p>Unmodified signed binaries, benchmark source 06c81a5 / product a5d4af4. Screenpipe default PII removal is disabled for exact raw-text admission; OSwind import builds unused local vectors. Shipping semantics, response shape and caches differ. No matched ingestion, natural capture/audio quality, physical power or overall ranking follows. Earlier setup added task-only Spotlight exclusions; restoration remains unverified. A separate native collector CI detach failure also remains unresolved.</p>'
keyword=json.loads((ROOT/'benchmarks/keyword-scope-scale-v1.json').read_text())
keyword_rows=''.join(f'<tr><td>{run["rows"]:,}</td><td>{esc(case)}</td><td>{summary["baseline"]["searchMS"]["medianMS"]:.3f} ms</td><td>{summary["candidate"]["searchMS"]["medianMS"]:.3f} ms</td><td>{summary["baseline"]["searchMS"]["p95MS"]:.3f} / {summary["candidate"]["searchMS"]["p95MS"]:.3f} ms</td></tr>' for run in keyword['independentReview']['scale'] for case,summary in run['report']['summary'].items())
keyword_table='<h3>OSwind: required phrases and Boolean query scaling</h3><p>Signed prior 793574e versus '+esc(keyword['source'][:7])+', eight authored cases at each size, five alternating timed rounds per case/profile plus warmup. All 288 scale responses retain exact paired results and original sources. Independent review checks authored ordering, RRF scores, returned fields, response hashes and timing quantiles. The full 40-stage local qualification passes. <a href="KEYWORD-CONSTRAINT-SCALE.md">Protocol and remaining work</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/keyword-scope-scale-v1.json">Receipt</a> · <a href="../benchmarks/keyword-scope-raw-v1.zip">Actual response files</a>.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table id="keyword-scale"><thead><tr><th>Sources</th><th>Query case</th><th>Prior median</th><th>Current median</th><th>Prior / current p95</th></tr></thead><tbody>'+keyword_rows+'</tbody></table></div><p>Times are product-reported search duration; CLI wall observations are retained separately. Five warm samples with uncontrolled caches/background activity do not establish a stable population tail. These authored text archives contain no indexed model; the hybrid row measures empty-model fallback. No broad semantic/speaker-heavy scaling, capture/ingestion, GPU efficiency, physical energy, complete sync, distribution or competitor-ranking acceptance follows. The older stock Screenpipe workload remains separate.</p>'
feature_rows=''.join(f'<tr data-status="{esc(f["status"])}"><td>{f["id"]}</td><td>{esc(f["axis"])}</td><td><strong>{esc(f["feature"])}</strong><small>{esc(f["references"])}</small></td><td><span class="status {"good" if f["status"] in ["tested","live verified"] else ""}">{esc(f["status"])}</span></td><td>{esc(f["evidence"])}</td></tr>' for f in features)
page='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>OSwind — Desktop memory landscape & parity ledger</title><style>
:root{color-scheme:light;--bg:#f4f5f0;--ink:#172b2b;--muted:#526564;--line:#d5dcd5;--accent:#16654e}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:var(--bg);color:var(--ink);font:15px/1.6 system-ui,-apple-system,sans-serif}a{color:var(--accent);text-underline-offset:3px}button,input,select{font:inherit}button{cursor:pointer}button,a,input,select{outline-offset:4px}header{padding:60px max(24px,calc((100vw - 1240px)/2)) 36px;background:#172e2a;color:#f1f8ee}h1{font-size:clamp(32px,5vw,62px);line-height:1.05;max-width:900px;letter-spacing:-2px;margin:18px 0 24px}header p{max-width:850px;color:#c9dcd2}.eyebrow{font:600 11px ui-monospace,monospace;letter-spacing:1px;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted)}header .eyebrow{color:#99d7ba}nav{position:sticky;top:0;z-index:2;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:20px;padding:13px 24px;background:#f4f5f0ed;backdrop-filter:blur(10px);border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}main{max-width:1288px;margin:auto;padding:0 24px 80px}section{padding-top:45px;scroll-margin-top:70px}h2{font-size:30px;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:-.6px}h3{font-size:23px;line-height:1.2;margin:9px 0 17px}.callout{padding:20px 24px;border-left:4px solid var(--accent);background:#e3ece3;border-radius:0 9px 9px 0}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:18px}.vendor{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:14px;padding:24px;background:#fff}.price{background:#eef3eb;border-radius:8px;padding:12px;font-weight:600;font-size:13px}dt{font:600 10px ui-monospace,monospace;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted);letter-spacing:.8px;margin-top:14px}dd{margin:4px 0 0}footer{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:16px;margin-top:18px;font-size:12px}.table-wrap{overflow-x:auto;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:10px}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:13px;background:#fff;min-width:850px}th{text-align:left;font-size:10px;letter-spacing:1px;text-transform:uppercase;background:#e4ebe2}th,td{padding:13px 14px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);vertical-align:top}td:first-child{font:11px ui-monospace,monospace;color:var(--muted)}small{display:block;color:var(--muted);margin-top:5px}.status{display:inline-block;padding:3px 8px;background:#f8edd3;border-radius:5px;font-size:11px;white-space:nowrap}.good{background:#dceddd;color:#17543d}.tools{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:12px;margin:18px 0}.tools input{flex:1;min-width:180px}input,select,button{padding:9px 12px;border:1px solid #aabdb1;background:white;border-radius:7px;color:var(--ink)}p{max-width:1000px}code{font-size:12px;background:#e3e9df;padding:3px 5px;border-radius:4px}ul{padding-left:22px}li{margin:7px 0}.steps{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:16px}.steps>div{background:white;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;padding:20px}@media(max-width:760px){.grid,.steps{grid-template-columns:1fr}header{padding-top:38px}nav{gap:12px;font-size:12px}.vendor{padding:19px}main{padding-inline:16px}h2{font-size:26px}}@media print{nav,.tools{display:none}body{background:white}.vendor{break-inside:avoid}header{color:#172b2b;background:white;padding:20px}header p,header .eyebrow{color:#526564}}
</style></head><body><header><div class="eyebrow">OSwind / research & delivery notebook / '''+esc(landscape['reviewed'])+'''</div><h1>A memory for your Mac.<br>A measurable path to parity.</h1><p>Screen history, conversations, local intelligence and useful recall. This report compares '''+str(len(vendors))+''' relevant products and projects, then turns their capabilities into an explicit OSwind delivery ledger.</p><p>Research snapshot: primary publisher documentation. Feature descriptions are vendor claims unless a test is explicitly identified. OSwind is an initial implementation; feature-complete and top-three claims are not established.</p></header><nav aria-label="Sections"><a href="#thesis">What matters</a><a href="#offerings">Offerings & plans</a><a href="#parity">Parity ledger</a><a href="#benchmarks">Benchmarks</a><a href="#roadmap">Build priorities</a><a href="#method">Method & caveats</a></nav><main>
<section id="thesis"><h2>There are three different products hiding in this category.</h2><div class="steps"><div><h3>Replay what you saw</h3><p>Original Rewind, ScreenMemory, Rewind Desktop, rem, Retrace and OpenRecall emphasize screenshots/video, OCR, a visual timeline and source recovery.</p></div><div><h3>Remember what you worked on</h3><p>Screenpipe, Pieces, Littlebird, TimeScroll, Minne, OpenHistory, silverfish and Goldfish add contextual retrieval, assistants, recaps, routines and integrations. Several use foreground text without screenshots. Local capture and local inference are separate decisions.</p></div><div><h3>Remember what was said</h3><p>Limitless, Omi and Granola prioritize speech, speaker context, notes and actions. Full desktop parity requires both visual and audio evidence.</p></div></div><p class="callout"><strong>OSwind’s product direction:</strong> native Mac capture and evidence browsing; local inference as a first-class path; BYOK without lock-in; explicit data controls; performance measured across active capture, idle, retrieval and model loading. Native implementation helps but is not proof of better power use.</p></section>
<section id="offerings"><h2>Offerings, plans and differences</h2><p>Prices below are the reviewed page defaults, in USD where shown. Annual equivalents are labeled; optional provider/API charges and hardware are separate. Current pages supersede older blog/listicle amounts.</p><div class="grid">'''+cards+'''</div></section>
<section id="parity"><h2>OSwind feature ledger</h2><p>This is a union of meaningful desktop capabilities, not a claim every vendor offers every row. “Implemented” means code exists; “tested” means focused automated coverage; “live verified” identifies a real runtime check. Full end-to-end and cross-device validation are separate gates.</p><div class="tools"><input id="filter" aria-label="Filter feature ledger" placeholder="Filter features, apps, gaps…"><select id="status" aria-label="Filter by status"><option value="">All statuses</option>'''+''.join(f'<option>{esc(s)}</option>' for s in sorted({f['status'] for f in features}))+'''</select><button id="copy">Copy visible TODOs as Markdown</button></div><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>ID</th><th>Axis</th><th>Feature / references</th><th>OSwind status</th><th>Evidence / gap</th></tr></thead><tbody id="rows">'''+feature_rows+'''</tbody></table></div><p id="count" aria-live="polite"></p></section>
<section id="benchmarks"><h2>Measure the system people actually leave running.</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Axis</th><th>Protocol</th><th>What is known now</th><th>What must not be claimed</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Retrieval</td><td>Same corpus and relevance labels; Recall@5, MRR, no-result accuracy; p50/p95 including embedding.</td><td>Authored 32-document/35-query suite: Qwen3 hybrid Recall@5/MRR 1.0 on 31 answerable queries, p95 ~92 ms; Apple hybrid Recall@5 .871/MRR .720, p95 ~4.7 ms. All 4 no-evidence queries returned candidates.</td><td>Small fixture used for ranking tuning; long-source passage regressions are authored too. Independent multilingual evaluation and answer abstention remain open. This is not a competitor win.</td></tr><tr><td>Capture / OCR</td><td>Fixed fonts/scales/languages, small text, moving windows, private fixtures; OCR CER/WER, missed transitions, index lag.</td><td>Vision synthetic OCR ~270 ms; real targeted window ingest ~0.49–0.67 s. Live secret-image suppression, app/title exclusion and delete checks pass. Foreground/browser transitions remain open.</td><td>Configured cadence does not prove capture completeness or OCR fidelity.</td></tr><tr><td>Power / storage</td><td>Same Mac/profile/brightness/workload; idle, active, meeting, low battery; CPU/RSS, disk bytes/hour, watts over time.</td><td>Paused debug process sampled separately. No 24h capture/power result yet.</td><td>Vendor compression numbers and snapshot estimates are not comparable measured results.</td></tr><tr><td>Audio / models</td><td>Fixed speech fixture, WER and real-time factor; model cold/warm latency, GPU execution evidence; silence/noise tests.</td><td>Apple Intelligence fixture answer ~0.8s. Ollama qwen3:4b answered in ~3.8s warm sample with 100% GPU; Whisper matched the public JFK fixture.</td><td>Backend support alone is not proof of an executed GPU path or diarization quality.</td></tr><tr><td>Competitors</td><td>Pin versions, identical workloads/retention/features; allow publisher default and tuned profiles; preserve raw metrics.</td><td>Pinned MIT rem database-method comparison on synthetic text: at 100k rows rem keyword p95 .454 ms versus OSwind 7.045 ms. OSwind loses this workload. Stock Screenpipe keyword HTTP is now measured below; whole competitor capture, audio and power remain unmeasured.</td><td>No overall top-three ranking or superiority claim is justified.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>'''+component_table+keyword_table+'''</section>
<section id="roadmap"><h2>Build priorities that move the whole product forward</h2><ol><li><strong>Close correctness boundaries:</strong> lock/startup/pause, privacy context across in-flight work, raw-media handling, transactional imports, cancellation and storage pressure. Verify live browser/audio behavior.</li><li><strong>Make recall trustworthy:</strong> extend the delivered local GPU embeddings with multimodal retrieval, natural-language dates, query highlighting, evidence citations and a diverse gold retrieval set. Keep keyword mode available.</li><li><strong>Finish daily-use workflows:</strong> extend delivered durable chats, meeting sessions, short audio flush, diarization, timed pause, scheduled routines, Markdown/media exports and migration.</li><li><strong>Prove sustained performance:</strong> 10k/100k/1m retrieval scaling, capture-content benchmarks, all-night soak, disk-growth and physical power measurements. Add ANN and hardware video compression only with evidence.</li><li><strong>Close polish/security parity:</strong> vault/Touch ID, accessibility/focus review, browser and older-macOS matrix, notarized installer, crash recovery, update channel and repeatable competitor runs.</li></ol><p>Personal device sync remains required for the requested desktop parity. Its internal causal journal and encrypted object transport are in progress; automatic library adapters, pairing, public setup and actual two-Mac/provider acceptance remain open. <a href="PERSONAL-SYNC.md">Complete sync requirements</a>. Team controls, enterprise governance and cross-platform clients remain separately labeled outside the current desktop delivery scope.</p></section>
<section id="method"><h2>Method and limits</h2><p>The initial 16 profiles were reviewed October 22, with documentation rechecks and four additional profiles on October 29, 2026, America/Los_Angeles. Each card labels its source check, unavailable pages and unresolved current prices. Publisher/cache snapshots can lag current software; documentation does not establish delivered runtime behavior. Implementation evidence keeps its source revision. Sources are linked in each product card. No vendor marketing benchmark was adopted as an independent measurement. Product code is independently implemented. An isolated comparison harness compiles pinned MIT rem database methods in ignored build folders, retaining its license; no rem source is embedded in the product. License names describe reviewed repositories and do not constitute a compatibility audit.</p><p>Original Rewind/Limitless and rewind.app are distinct products. Historical wind-down announcements are separate from current availability; the original homepage was unavailable during the October 29 recheck. Two unrelated projects are named Retrace. Pensieve was previously named Memos. These naming collisions matter when evaluating downloads and feature claims.</p><p>Publisher pages can disagree. Screenpipe’s current onboarding table is used for annual plans; its commercial-source requirements are preserved. Pieces’ current page supersedes older free-tier summaries. Free-tier inconsistencies on ScreenMemory/Omi are flagged. Enterprise compliance statements are publisher claims, not reviewed certifications.</p><p>Local-only means all selected processing remains local: OCR, transcription, embeddings, inference, storage, sync and connected-client behavior must each be checked. OSwind’s optional BYOK path intentionally sends selected text to the configured provider. Pattern-based redaction is incomplete protection.</p><p>Native sample layouts and report filtering were visually reviewed; targeted synthetic capture passed while unlocked. An unlocked native session verified model preparation, strategy selection and semantic search. Native sample calendar/hour-to-Ask/citation, Escape and Command-K checks pass on the signed 0118243 candidate. Real generated-tone system audio passes production inventory/decoder tests in normal and Thread Sanitizer runs, with explicit hidden-source identities. Actual signed-GUI/controller/ASR and microphone capture, broader live setup, shortcuts during capture and foreground/browser transitions remain open gates. This report and its machine-readable companion are maintained project artifacts, not a completion certificate.</p></section></main><script>
const rows=[...document.querySelectorAll('#rows tr')],q=document.querySelector('#filter'),s=document.querySelector('#status'),count=document.querySelector('#count');function apply(){let n=0;for(const row of rows){const match=row.textContent.toLowerCase().includes(q.value.toLowerCase())&&(!s.value||row.dataset.status===s.value);row.hidden=!match;if(match)n++}count.textContent=n+' of '+rows.length+' requirements shown';document.querySelector('#copy').textContent='Copy visible TODOs as Markdown'}q.addEventListener('input',apply);s.addEventListener('change',apply);apply();document.querySelector('#copy').addEventListener('click',async()=>{const text=rows.filter(r=>!r.hidden&&!['tested','live verified','out of v0 desktop scope'].includes(r.dataset.status)).map(r=>'- [ ] '+r.cells[0].textContent+' '+r.cells[2].querySelector('strong').textContent+' — '+r.cells[4].textContent).join('\\n');try{await navigator.clipboard.writeText(text);document.querySelector('#copy').textContent='Copied'}catch{window.prompt('Copy TODOs',text)}});
</script></body></html>'''
(ROOT/'docs/landscape.html').write_text(page)
print(f'Rendered {len(vendors)} offerings and {len(features)} requirements')
